    "done_when": "Pose the certificate exterior on the exact analytic support, as followup f-cfs-exterior-on-exact-support on converged-forward-solve states.\n\nThe certificate's prescribed exterior subtracts an analytic-density image integrated on the production spline-clipped support (_analytic_profile_support, scripts/analytic_oracle_fixtures/measure.py near line 1028). It leaves a closure residual of 0.0062, 0.0177 and 0.0111 at 550, 2,098 and 5,158 cells even with exact support, which masks the map's own booking error (0.0249, 0.0090, 0.0044). The census also flags that _exterior_cache_identity (measure.py near line 1133) hard-codes the clip string, so a support change would silently reuse a stale exterior cache.\n\nDone when:\n(1) The fixture's prescribed exterior is computed from the independently integrated analytic density on the exact analytic support. Reuse scripts/prototypes/support/geometry.py analytic_polygons and the fixture's exact_current_moments.\n(2) The exterior cache identity carries the support arm and the polygonanalytic.py revision, so no stale exterior is reused.\n(3) With the exact support arm, the exterior closure term at about 550, 2,000 and 5,000 cells falls below the booking term at every rung. Report both, together with the map relative sup.\n(4) The legacy-support arm at 550 diverted cells still reproduces 0.197327, through an explicitly named legacy exterior, as the positive control.\n(5) Negative control: the old spline-support exterior brings the closure residual back at 2,000 cells by test id.\n(6) Add tests/test_certificate_exterior_support.py.\n(7) Write an evidence fragment, docs/evidence/fragments/converged-forward-solve/cfs-exterior-exact-support.html, with plan-evidence-for converged-forward-solve; reckon audit-doc reports 0 errors.\n\nEdit only scripts/analytic_oracle_fixtures, the new test and the fragment; do not edit nova/.\n\nRun conditions: H200 rows run as one job through RECKON_ALLOW_NESTED_LAUNCH=1 scripts/h200_test_lane/run.sh --log (an absolute path in the run directory) --wait -- (targets), or one sbatch job on --partition=betelgeuse --reservation=gpu_0003_grpA --gres=gpu:1 with rungs as rows inside the allocation (never an array), --time sized to finish, XLA_PYTHON_CLIENT_PREALLOCATE=false and TMPDIR=/tmp in the submit environment and in every child; submit for real and read squeue a minute later rather than trusting sbatch --test-only. On a compute node run /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/nova/.venv/bin/python directly with PYTHONPATH set to the run worktree and never invoke uv; every login-node uv command carries --no-sync and nothing runs uv sync. configure_dtypes() before any array and jax_enable_x64 asserted True. Gates pass by delta against orientation_base_sha in per-module fresh processes, both arms running the same test files with the repository root conftest, baseline_suite and after_suite as single-line JSON whose log_path names one log file and whose command is literally runnable. Any wait is declared on the job that finishes last as wait_probe [\"sacct\",\"-n\",\"-X\",\"-P\",\"-j\",\"(job id)\",\"-o\",\"State\"] and wait_terminal [\"COMPLETED\",\"FAILED\",\"CANCELLED\",\"TIMEOUT\",\"OUT_OF_MEMORY\",\"NODE_FAIL\"] as JSON lists, and names every job it depends on in wait_condition. The certified 550, 2,000 and 5,000-cell machines and exteriors are cached under /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/runs/r-20261009T181553786165-proto-support/ordered/rows/cache and may be read in place, never written. Run filepath relativize over any evidence fragment before committing. Commit with conventional subjects and bodies at every step and write the manifest and commit before every job wait; the manifest commits line lists every commit; status is complete, blocked or failed, which the worker sets itself. No plan labels in source names or comments.",
